          "nudge_reason": null,
          "final_text_tail": " and compute in `__init__` using `model_post_init` semantics. But pydantic BaseModel `__init__` with mutable assignment is blocked in v2 unless `model_config = ConfigDict(...)`. Simplest robust approach: keep them as fields, compute and assign in a `model_post_init`.\n\nRevised `ToolCall`:\n```python\n    class ToolCall(BaseModel):\n        name: str\n        args: dict[str, Any]\n        fingerprint: str = \"\"\n        id: str = \"\"\n\n        def model_post_init(self, __context):\n            canonical_args = _canonicalize_tool_call_args(self.args)\n            canonical = {\"name\": self.name, \"args\": canonical_args}\n            serialized = json.dumps(canonical, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n            digest = hashlib.sha256(serialized.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n            self.fingerprint = digest\n            self.id = digest[:8]\n```\n\nThis requires pydantic to allow assignment after init (pydantic v2 BaseModel allows attribute assignment if `model_config = ConfigDict(validate_assignment=False)` which is default; assignment works unless `frozen`). This is the correct, idiomatic solution.\n\nI cannot apply these edits because no file-writing tool is available in this environment.\n\nI don't have a tool available to edit files (only glob, grep, read, skill). The environment has no write/edit/bash tool exposed, so I'm unable to modify `dspy/adapters/types/tool.py` directly. The implementation above is the exact change required; no human or further tooling is available to apply it.",
